### Static Polymorphism

#### binds trait to concrete class

- Verify: binds trait to concrete class


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 20 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-CLASSES-001
step("Verify: binds trait to concrete class")
trait Logger:
    fn log(self, msg: text) -> text

class ConsoleLogger:
    fn log(self, msg: text) -> text:
        return "Console: " + msg

bind Logger = ConsoleLogger

fn create_logger() -> Logger:
    return ConsoleLogger {}

val logger: Logger = create_logger()
val res = logger.log("Hello")
var result = 0
if res == "Console: Hello":
    result = 1
expect result == 1
```

</details>

#### binds trait with multiple methods

- Verify: binds trait with multiple methods


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 16 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-CLASSES-001
step("Verify: binds trait with multiple methods")
trait Calculator:
    fn add(self, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
    fn multiply(self, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64

class SimpleCalc:
    fn add(self, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64:
        return a + b
    fn multiply(self, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64:
        return a * b

bind Calculator = SimpleCalc

val calc: Calculator = SimpleCalc {}
expect calc.add(3, 4) + calc.multiply(2, 5) == 17
```

</details>

